everity": "SEV3", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "Deployed hotfix v2.3.2 to all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), replacing v2.3.1. v2.3.1 was unhealthy with an 18% error rate. v2.3.2 had never been released to production before, so change-manager approval was required and granted before the rollout. After the deploy, the service is healthy with a 0.2% error rate. Rollback target if needed: v2.3.0 (last healthy release).", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.2-hotfix-deploy"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 179355, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01E7LiTvSPPEgCcY2r5fARAC", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.2-hotfix-deploy", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 179355, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01E7LiTvSPPEgCcY2r5fARAC", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 182870, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I deployed the checkout-api hotfix v2.3.2 to all production regions (us-east, us-west and eu-west). The service is now healthy and its error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n\n- **Approval:** v2.3.2 had never been released to production before, so policy required change-manager approval. The deploy went to the change-manager automatically, who approved it before it rolled out.\n- **What it replaced:** v2.3.1, which was unhealthy everywhere with an 18% error rate.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV3 incident **INC-0001** for checkout-api to record the change, which paged on-call. It notes that v2.3.0, the last healthy release, is the version to roll back to if needed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thi