_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I deployed the checkout-api hotfix v2.3.2 to all production regions (us-east, us-west and eu-west). The service is now healthy and its error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n\n- **Approval:** v2.3.2 had never been released to production before, so policy required change-manager approval. The deploy went to the change-manager automatically, who approved it before it rolled out.\n- **What it replaced:** v2.3.1, which was unhealthy everywhere with an 18% error rate.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV3 incident **INC-0001** for checkout-api to record the change, which paged on-call. It notes that v2.3.0, the last healthy release, is the version to roll back to if needed.", "type": "text"}]}]}